{#-
  Purpose: Determine whether Rock's IdKey (the obfuscated id used in Sign-Up
  Register URLs, e.g. ProjectId=bg31BgMbYo) is reachable from Lava.

  Context: the Sign-Up Finder generates
    /page/3718?ProjectId=<IdKey>&LocationId=<IdKey>&ScheduleId=<IdKey>
  IdKey is computed in C# and cannot be produced by SQL. If raw integer ids
  are NOT accepted by the Sign-Up Register block, the public sign-up pages
  must obtain IdKey through RockEntity Lava instead.

  HOW TO RUN: paste into any HTML Content block on a page you can view, and
  set the block's "Enabled Lava Commands" to include RockEntity.
  Delete the block afterwards — this is a scratch probe.

  WHAT TO REPORT BACK: the rendered output of all four tests below.

  Test data = Kids Min Orientation, 8/27 opportunity:
    GroupId 345104 | LocationId 36682 | ScheduleId 3912
  Expected IdKeys if this works: ProjectId=bg31BgMbYo (group 345104)
-#}

<h3>IdKey Lava Probe</h3>

<h4>Test 1 — Group by id (singular form)</h4>
{% group id:'345104' %}
  Name: {{ group.Name }}<br>
  Id: {{ group.Id }}<br>
  IdKey: <strong>{{ group.IdKey }}</strong><br>
  (expected IdKey: bg31BgMbYo)
{% endgroup %}

<h4>Test 2 — Group by where (collection form)</h4>
{% group where:'Id == 345104' %}
  {% for g in groupItems %}
    Name: {{ g.Name }} | Id: {{ g.Id }} | IdKey: <strong>{{ g.IdKey }}</strong><br>
  {% endfor %}
{% endgroup %}

<h4>Test 3 — Location</h4>
{% location id:'36682' %}
  Name: {{ location.Name }}<br>
  Id: {{ location.Id }}<br>
  IdKey: <strong>{{ location.IdKey }}</strong><br>
  (expected IdKey: Vm3W4JoY7r)
{% endlocation %}

<h4>Test 4 — Schedule</h4>
{% schedule id:'3912' %}
  Id: {{ schedule.Id }}<br>
  IdKey: <strong>{{ schedule.IdKey }}</strong><br>
  (expected IdKey: z0YnJDwYXo)
{% endschedule %}

<hr>
<p><em>If IdKey renders empty or blank in every test, it is not exposed to Lava
and the Register link must be built another way (e.g. keeping the stock Finder's
generated URLs, or a lightweight lookup block).</em></p>
